/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 79 0 R
/T (Physical AI refers to software embedded in robots and machines that can perceive through cameras, force sensors or tactile systems; interpret situations; act on objects; and learn from data, demonstrations or simulation. Generative AI mainly produces digital content. Traditional industrial robots usually repeat pre-programmed motions in controlled cells. Physical AI tries to preserve that precision while coping with variation in the real world.)
/E (Physical AI refers to software embedded in robots and machines that can perceive through cameras, force sensors or tactile systems; interpret situations; act on objects; and learn from data, demonstrations or simulation. Generative AI mainly produces digital content. Traditional industrial robots usually repeat pre-programmed motions in controlled cells. Physical AI tries to preserve that precision while coping with variation in the real world.)
