/E (Europe has strong research institutes, machinery companies and industrial customers, but less late-stage capital and a fragmented market. Its own automation demand also weakened last year. According to the IFR, EU installations fell 11 per cent in 2025 to 60,500 units; Germany installed 24,842 \(down 8 per cent\) and Italy about 7,800 \(down 11 per cent\). The IFR expects European installations to be flat in 2026.)
