/Title (In humanoids the lead is starker. IDC estimates that almost 25,000 humanoid robots were shipped worldwide in the first half of 2026, up 432 per cent year on year, with Chinese vendors building more than 95 per cent of them; AgiBot shipped about 8,600 and Unitree about 5,000, while Figure AI shipped a few dozen. Another count, reported by TechNode, put shipments at about 19,100 units and the Chinese share above 97 per cent. The totals differ by method; the direction does not.)
/Dest [16 0 R /Fit]
